# Registry recovery drill — 2026-10-19 (A5 evidence, local)

Question (docs/audit-2026-10-19.md A5): the live Litestream config
excluded metadata.sqlite (the registry: credential hashes, scopes,
database rows), so from the bucket alone every scoped key was lost.
Sandbox gate 11 had proved the registry file round-trips through a
bucket with the gateway STOPPED first. This drill proves the harder,
production-shaped claim: the registry can be replicated continuously
while the gateway serves, because registry connections in the gateway
are per-operation (src/store.rs), the same profile as the application
databases already replicated live.

scripts/registry-recovery-drill.sh, run twice, both PASS (file://
replica as bucket stand-in, pinned litestream 0.5.17; the rendered
config now carries the metadata entry plus explicit
`retention: 168h` / `snapshot-interval: 24h`, which litestream
accepted and replicated under):

  1 ok: replication running against the live gateway, registry included
  2 ok: registry writes made under a live gateway reached the replica
       (a second scoped key minted AFTER replication started is polled
        for in restores of the registry replica until visible)
  3 ok: registry and data restored from the replica alone
       (data dir wiped; exact rows [(1,reg-alpha),(2,reg-bravo),
        (3,reg-charlie)], integrity_check ok on both files)
  4 ok: both pre-loss scoped keys authenticate with scope intact
       (read ledger_app = 3 rows; other_app refused for both keys)
  PASS

scripts/litestream-sync-drill.sh also still passes with the registry
entry in the render (create -> visible gap -> sync -> restored ->
delete -> unregistered).

Residues the policy records honestly (docs/recovery-policy.md):
- Restored-pair skew: registry and data replicate independently; a key
  or database created seconds before host loss may exist on only one
  side of a restored pair. The recovery runbook verifies `dg list` +
  key scopes after restore and re-issues anything inside the skew
  window; registry changes are rare admin events, so the window is
  narrow and detectable.
- Nothing here was run against micro2 or the real bucket. Live
  enablement (updated sync script -> registry enters the live config
  on the next timer fire) is an owner-approved step.
